{
  "reviewer": "Claude (Opus 5), 2026-10-02. Each value was translated back to English without the English original in view, then compared for meaning: a dropped clause, an inverted negation, a lost \"instead\". Two fixes came out of it — es accountRecipients.privacy.ownAccounts gained \"En cambio\" for English's \"instead\", and ja receive.privacy.publicAddress gained \"いずれかの\" for \"one of your Seedelfs\". NO NATIVE SPEAKER HAS READ THESE. That is the accepted risk (post-release roadmap, open question 2); a user who reports an error is the feedback loop working. Round two (Lovejoin's page, 2026-10-03) back-translated 34 more, the \"not mixed yet\" warning and the seed's among them. No correction came out of the Spanish pass this round; lovejoin.warn.notMixed.number_other is a bare {{count}}, recorded as exact-reuse. Round three (Minswap's swap screens, 2026-10-03) back-translated 16 more, the quote's and the Lovejoin switch's privacy notes among them. No correction came out of the Spanish pass this round. Round four (the connector's window and a site's session, 2026-10-03) back-translated 17 more, what each connection lets a site learn among them. No correction came out of the Spanish pass this round. Round five (the review fixes, 2026-10-03) back-translated 13 more: a dApp's staking certificates as whole sentences (dappUi.cert.warn.*), pool.warn.retiringSoon and claim.warn.skippedItem; no correction came out of the Spanish pass, claim.warn.skippedItem is a bare {{name}}: {{why}}. recorded as exact-reuse, and the reviewer is still Claude and no native speaker has read them. Round six (the whole-locale review's corrections, 2026-10-03): 28 critical keys (36 values, plural forms counted) were corrected and back-translated again, among them mint.privacy.fromPrivate, which had read as payments you sent to other people's Seedelfs and now says Seedelf payments other people made to you, the three removal warnings that kept the English \"mint\" (now \"acuñación\"), lovejoin.privacy.hides, whose subject was an English indirect question, and the three dApp notes whose \"ella\" pointed at the wrong noun; the reviewer is still Claude and no native speaker has read them. A second reader then checked every value the round changed and back-translated the 49 critical ones blind again: no critical error, and one agreement fix on a critical key came out of it (dappUi.warn.unknownInputs_one now says \"que no lo gasta\" for its one UTxO). Round seven (the code fixes after the cross-area review, 2026-10-04): lockFailed.warn.message now ends the reason it quotes with a full stop of its own (\"{{message}}. Vuelve a intentarlo\"), so a browser's message without one no longer runs into the next sentence, and it was back-translated blind again with no change in meaning; the reviewer is still Claude and no native speaker has read it.",
